1
00:00:05,335 --> 00:00:09,158
[SPEAKER_00]: So, some people say that we only live once.

2
00:00:10,078 --> 00:00:14,021
[SPEAKER_00]: So, we must enjoy our lives to the fullest.

3
00:00:14,061 --> 00:00:16,003
[SPEAKER_00]: Do whatever makes us happy.

4
00:00:16,903 --> 00:00:19,825
[SPEAKER_00]: Go after our desires.

5
00:00:19,845 --> 00:00:22,648
[SPEAKER_00]: Try to achieve what we want to achieve.

6
00:00:24,185 --> 00:00:24,846
[SPEAKER_00]: Really enjoy it.

7
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:26,607
[SPEAKER_00]: You only live once.

8
00:00:26,647 --> 00:00:29,229
[SPEAKER_00]: What do you... what do you say to this?

9
00:00:29,249 --> 00:00:37,675
[SPEAKER_00]: This idea.

10
00:00:41,558 --> 00:00:41,998
[SPEAKER_01]: It's okay.

11
00:00:42,078 --> 00:00:42,278
[SPEAKER_01]: Come on.

12
00:00:42,298 --> 00:00:42,839
[SPEAKER_01]: A bit late.

13
00:00:42,919 --> 00:00:43,319
[SPEAKER_01]: Go down.

14
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:53,907
[SPEAKER_01]: The eh... Well, you...

15
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,661
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're an authentic person...

16
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:58,742
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, many people say that as a form of dismissal.

17
00:00:59,503 --> 00:01:00,283
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah, you only live once.

18
00:01:00,764 --> 00:01:02,064
[SPEAKER_01]: There's nothing you can say to them.

19
00:01:02,765 --> 00:01:09,489
[SPEAKER_01]: But, say, if people start doubting that notion of you only live once, the fact is you don't really know how many times you live.

20
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:12,611
[SPEAKER_01]: It's as simple as that.

21
00:01:12,991 --> 00:01:13,691
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't know.

22
00:01:14,172 --> 00:01:14,852
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot know.

23
00:01:15,553 --> 00:01:17,634
[SPEAKER_00]: There are people who believe they live only once.

24
00:01:17,754 --> 00:01:19,815
[SPEAKER_00]: There are people who believe that you live many times.

25
00:01:20,556 --> 00:01:21,957
[SPEAKER_01]: There are people who believe you live twice.

26
00:01:22,981 --> 00:01:25,322
[SPEAKER_01]: Such as rebirthing heaven or hell and that's it.

27
00:01:26,123 --> 00:01:28,644
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, it's always going to remain a matter of belief.

28
00:01:30,305 --> 00:01:41,251
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're somebody who's trying to help yourself in an ultimate manner, who want to develop your mind and so on, you would... you have to recognize that and admit that it's always going to be a matter of belief.

29
00:01:43,172 --> 00:01:48,435
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you're sure, when you feel completely confident in saying you live only once, well, that's not true.

30
00:01:49,752 --> 00:01:57,558
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you don't know for sure, yet you being sure, based upon a mere belief, it's a... it's a... it's an... it's a... it's a big mistake.

31
00:01:58,698 --> 00:01:59,839
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a very risky thing to do.

32
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,882
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I'm not saying you should stop believing whatever you're believing.

33
00:02:04,022 --> 00:02:07,745
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm just saying you have to recognize that it is a belief and it cannot be more than that.

34
00:02:08,805 --> 00:02:14,249
[SPEAKER_01]: So, from that point of view, then you recognize, well, what is the safest belief I can have?

35
00:02:14,269 --> 00:02:17,852
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, if I live only once, if I believe that, okay, sure,

36
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:22,921
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, as a result of that belief, I end up behaving in this life whichever way I want.

37
00:02:23,821 --> 00:02:26,362
[SPEAKER_01]: But, what if... what if you live more than once?

38
00:02:28,842 --> 00:02:32,983
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, because of your bad behavior in this life, you end up paying the price.

39
00:02:33,423 --> 00:02:42,646
[SPEAKER_01]: Because those people who do believe in future lives, be it Christians or Buddhists or Hindus, they believe that you're gonna be reborn accordingly to your actions.

40
00:02:42,686 --> 00:02:43,366
[SPEAKER_01]: Even Christians.

41
00:02:43,446 --> 00:02:47,847
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, if you... if you are not a good Christian, heaven... heaven's doors will be closed to you.

42
00:02:48,689 --> 00:02:49,970
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you recognize that...

43
00:02:50,010 --> 00:02:55,755
[SPEAKER_01]: So, okay, so the belief of more lives requires a certain degree of good behavior.

44
00:02:57,676 --> 00:03:02,040
[SPEAKER_01]: In the sense of, if you don't behave well, your future lives is going to be... they're going to be very compromised.

45
00:03:03,873 --> 00:03:04,874
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's all you have to do.

46
00:03:04,894 --> 00:03:05,694
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't have to go further now.

47
00:03:05,714 --> 00:03:07,195
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't have to look for a proof.

48
00:03:07,215 --> 00:03:08,536
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to recognize it.

49
00:03:08,776 --> 00:03:09,376
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a belief.

50
00:03:10,036 --> 00:03:15,159
[SPEAKER_01]: And as such, the best belief for you to adopt is the one that's safest in the long run.

51
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,701
[SPEAKER_01]: As with everything else in the life, you don't want to think just for tomorrow.

52
00:03:19,322 --> 00:03:20,602
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I'll just steal this today.

53
00:03:21,063 --> 00:03:21,743
[SPEAKER_01]: Enjoy the money.

54
00:03:24,445 --> 00:03:24,805
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

55
00:03:25,005 --> 00:03:26,366
[SPEAKER_01]: Enjoy the money I stole tomorrow.

56
00:03:26,426 --> 00:03:28,467
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, the day after tomorrow, I'm going to go to jail for the rest of my life.

57
00:03:29,537 --> 00:03:31,479
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a very unwise thing to do.

58
00:03:32,139 --> 00:03:44,569
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in the same manner, you recognize there might be only one life, there might be more lives, but I should assume that there are more lives, in case that there are more lives, and then I end up paying the price for my misbehavior in this life.

59
00:03:45,469 --> 00:03:45,850
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's it.

60
00:03:46,070 --> 00:03:50,433
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's not exactly that you need to relinquish this life in order to gain heaven in future lives.

61
00:03:51,474 --> 00:03:54,577
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to not behave like an animal in this life.

62
00:03:54,717 --> 00:03:55,057
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

63
00:03:55,077 --> 00:03:57,279
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to be a... have a degree of virtue.

64
00:03:57,459 --> 00:03:58,760
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what everybody agrees upon.

65
00:04:00,911 --> 00:04:03,314
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what is the safest route for you to go?

66
00:04:03,414 --> 00:04:07,138
[SPEAKER_01]: It's basically to believe that there are probably more lives, just in case.

67
00:04:07,559 --> 00:04:08,841
[SPEAKER_01]: If they're not, so be it.

68
00:04:09,101 --> 00:04:10,342
[SPEAKER_01]: You behaved well in this life.

69
00:04:10,943 --> 00:04:12,545
[SPEAKER_01]: People praised you.

70
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:13,406
[SPEAKER_01]: You were trustworthy.

71
00:04:13,786 --> 00:04:15,288
[SPEAKER_00]: They trusted you.

72
00:04:16,029 --> 00:04:17,231
[SPEAKER_01]: They were never let down by you.

73
00:04:17,251 --> 00:04:20,815
[SPEAKER_01]: You were not a scoundrel, not stealing, whatever, cheating.

74
00:04:21,569 --> 00:04:27,592
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you behave properly, and you're rewarded right away, with respect, and people want to help you.

75
00:04:27,972 --> 00:04:34,195
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, if there were, if there are future lives, you're going to be rewarded even more, according to those who believe in that.

76
00:04:34,955 --> 00:04:36,136
[SPEAKER_01]: If not, well, so be it.

77
00:04:38,077 --> 00:04:40,278
[SPEAKER_01]: And this whole thing like, oh, I...

78
00:04:42,099 --> 00:04:44,940
[SPEAKER_01]: I need to... people should do whatever makes them happy.

79
00:04:48,138 --> 00:04:51,539
[SPEAKER_01]: Probably, about three quarters of people don't really know what makes them happy.

80
00:04:52,319 --> 00:04:59,140
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, for them, happiness is, eh... the experience... when... when they're not experiencing unhappiness.

81
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:06,441
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, for them, pursuit of happiness is actively running away from the prospect of unhappiness.

82
00:05:07,521 --> 00:05:12,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, your whole life revolves around running away from experiencing unpleasant feelings.

83
00:05:12,682 --> 00:05:14,082
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your definition of happiness.

84
00:05:14,763 --> 00:05:17,363
[SPEAKER_01]: Being... being on a constant... being constantly chased.

85
00:05:18,131 --> 00:05:19,431
[SPEAKER_01]: By unhappiness and anxiety.

86
00:05:21,492 --> 00:05:21,852
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

87
00:05:22,172 --> 00:05:22,512
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

88
00:05:23,093 --> 00:05:26,234
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what... that's what... that's what definition of happiness becomes for people.

89
00:05:26,574 --> 00:05:29,095
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's... if you look at it, that's exactly how people live their lives.

90
00:05:30,155 --> 00:05:45,620
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why there's so many, eh... like, issues in the modern society, like, with people with men... like, with mental problems, developing them, like, too much... too much pressure, too much stress, they can't deal with it, medications, everything else, vices, giving in to... to extreme measures, because you don't know what to do anymore.

91
00:05:46,883 --> 00:05:55,005
[SPEAKER_01]: You've proliferated in that escape so much and took it at its face value, but took it as as if it's sort of a good thing.

92
00:05:55,025 --> 00:05:56,386
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, you just do whatever makes you happy.

93
00:05:56,786 --> 00:05:57,486
[SPEAKER_01]: What makes me happy?

94
00:05:57,906 --> 00:06:00,307
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'm happy when I don't experience unhappiness.

95
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:01,867
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, what must I do?

96
00:06:01,927 --> 00:06:03,608
[SPEAKER_01]: I must prevent unhappiness at all cost.

97
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:05,961
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you become very stressed.

98
00:06:06,922 --> 00:06:10,986
[SPEAKER_01]: And then sensuality becomes the only mean of gaining some degree of happiness.

99
00:06:11,406 --> 00:06:12,327
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not happiness.

100
00:06:12,347 --> 00:06:14,209
[SPEAKER_01]: That's just management of your unhappiness.

101
00:06:14,709 --> 00:06:18,373
[SPEAKER_01]: Which, of course, from the point of view of that unhappiness, is happiness.

102
00:06:18,493 --> 00:06:19,854
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's a very relative happiness.

103
00:06:21,576 --> 00:06:23,578
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not really a happiness that can last.

104
00:06:24,899 --> 00:06:27,902
[SPEAKER_00]: But a happiness that lasts is one where you don't have to...

105
00:06:31,752 --> 00:06:32,112
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

106
00:06:32,132 --> 00:06:32,993
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

107
00:06:34,094 --> 00:06:46,085
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the happiness that lies, the happiness in itself, which means it's happiness of freedom, happiness of being above things that can affect you, not kind of happiness of necessity.

108
00:06:46,745 --> 00:06:49,808
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, I need to keep running away because this beast is chasing me.

109
00:06:51,189 --> 00:06:51,950
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not happiness.

110
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:56,474
[SPEAKER_01]: You might feel a relief when you feel like, oh, you're temporarily safe from the beast.

111
00:06:57,598 --> 00:07:02,419
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is happiness from the, obviously, the threat, the imminent threat of the beast attacking you.

112
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:07,121
[SPEAKER_01]: But overall, you're still not free from the beast, which means that's only a relative happiness.

113
00:07:07,821 --> 00:07:12,242
[SPEAKER_01]: And that beast is basically any form of suffering in this life.

114
00:07:12,282 --> 00:07:13,542
[SPEAKER_01]: Internal, external, any.

115
00:07:14,123 --> 00:07:18,064
[SPEAKER_01]: Anxiety, fear, stress, burden, loss.

116
00:07:19,424 --> 00:07:20,344
[SPEAKER_01]: Any, any of that.

117
00:07:20,524 --> 00:07:22,885
[SPEAKER_01]: It's basically an example.

118
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,161
[SPEAKER_01]: of the beast you're running away from.

119
00:07:26,021 --> 00:07:28,462
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the mind is just at its face value.

120
00:07:28,702 --> 00:07:31,644
[SPEAKER_01]: What it does when it experiences suffering, it turns away from it.

121
00:07:32,304 --> 00:07:33,485
[SPEAKER_01]: Wants to get rid of it.

122
00:07:34,385 --> 00:07:35,285
[SPEAKER_01]: Wants to prevent it.

123
00:07:37,106 --> 00:07:41,208
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, that becomes a definition of the purpose of your life.

124
00:07:41,548 --> 00:07:42,029
[SPEAKER_01]: Just running.

125
00:07:43,229 --> 00:07:47,271
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why people compulsively give in to the sensual desire.

126
00:07:47,531 --> 00:07:48,432
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not optional.

127
00:07:49,223 --> 00:07:51,124
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no matter... oh, I can...

128
00:07:51,184 --> 00:07:54,866
[SPEAKER_01]: I will refrain from sensuality today, unless the circumstances refrain you.

129
00:07:56,166 --> 00:08:00,649
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why... that's why it's not... it's not... it's almost mandatory for people to... Why?

130
00:08:00,689 --> 00:08:12,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they've... they chose the path of running away, which equals to say they chose the path of just taking their desires at the face value, which means they won't be able to... to resist them.

131
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:14,581
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where you're bound.

132
00:08:14,841 --> 00:08:19,566
[SPEAKER_01]: You're bound by the desire, you're bound by fear, you're bound by running away from suffering.

133
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:25,953
[SPEAKER_01]: So, any happiness that you can experience, it's going to be within that.

134
00:08:26,194 --> 00:08:29,037
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, it's a measly happiness.

